> I have a particularly lucky Samurai (haven't named him yet), who stumbled
> across a random wand of wishing in a non-wizard mode game.  I don't want to
> waste the wishes.  I'm looking for spoilers as to what I should wish for.

Hmm... what to wish for with an early wish is almost more a personal
choice then anything else.

I have found (to my dismay) that one of the surest ways of dying a slow
but spectacular death, is to wish for a powerful weapon.
You end up killing everything you see for the first while, and rocket
up into higher levels, before you actually have the defensive capabilities
to augment all that offense. And with higher levels come the tougher
monsters, which couldn't care one whit about your blessed +3 Stormbringer.  =)

If you get more then one wish, the choices become a bit easier...

First wish with a WoW is ALWAYS for '3 blessed scrolls of charging'
In your case, you already have one, so can skip this step.

If you're going to wish for a weapon, make sure you wish for armour to
back it up. Better choice is to make sure you have the armour first.
(You can always go for the weapon at your co-aligned altar)
and if you have problems with monsters to sacrifice, wish for a
cursed wand of create monster.  =)  It will do wonders.
(make sure you have a blessed luckstone when you try it)

First things first, quaff all blessed potions, read all blessed
scrolls (though you should watch out for that destroy armour scroll,
blessed or not)
Use the horn on the other potions, quaff all that aren't turned to water.
Rub the blessed lamp a few times, name it, to make sure the other lamp
is not the same (if they're different, one is a magic lamp, and thus another
potential wish)

My personal choices for armour, in order of preference:
 blessed rustproof +3 helm of telepathy
 blessed +3 shield of reflection
 blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail
 blessed rustproof +3 boots of speed
 blessed rustproof +3 gauntlets of dexterity

You already have telepathy from the amulet of ESP so the helmet isn't
neccessary, but you might want one eventually, so you can wear a different
amulet. Reflection will save your ass sooner then not, so go for the shield,
definitely. Magic resistance will do wonders too, but you could wait for this,
(and the crystal plate mail is pretty good for now)
The boots would do nice things (but make pets very annoying, unless you
have a wand of speed monster you can zap them (and yourself) with.

Usually you get the blessed/cursed status and the rustproof status you
wish for, I've found, but the + isn't always there...
So 3 blessed scrolls of enchant armour do would do well too.

Hmm.. ok.. you have at least 4 more wishes to use up (assuming the wand has
only 1 charge) at most 8 (if it has 3 charges, and both lamps are magic)

So, wish for...

(3 blessed scrolls of charging [already wished for])
blessed +3 shield of reflection
3 blessed scrolls of enchant armour
blessed rustproof +3 helm of telepathy
blessed amulet of life saving (you'll use it, I'm sure. And be thankful)

(thats five, if you get more, try for (your choice)...)
blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail
3 blessed scrolls of enchant weapon
3 blessed scrolls of genocide
3 blessed potions of gain ability
blessed rustproof +3 gauntlets of dexterity


*shrug* again, these are personal choices, and exact wishes would
be adjusted by your current level, dungeon level, stats and style
of play.


